{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>If he begets</b>. If he begets many sons. And the way of the holy tongue is to mention ten, and a hundred, and a thousand, for the reason that they are the totals of number. Do you not see that upon completing the ten you begin with one? Also seven is mentioned, and in its place I shall explain it." "<b>And many years he lives</b>. Until he is a old man." "<b>And though his days of years be many</b>. It is the way of the world." "<b>And also a burial</b>. The shrouds in which the dead person is buried." "<b>And the miscarriage</b>. It is a miscarried woman."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "The lemma reads יחיב, apparently a typographical error for יחיה; translated as though pointed יְחַיֶּה, 'he lives.'", 4 "Ibn Ezra reads הנפל as 'miscarried woman' (נפל אשה), i.e., a stillbirth; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:53.675042184Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}